+
+    G1.6 + G2.3: _build_weight_arena() packs every weight the optimized
+    forward actually reads (~63MB: the FP16 attention fold, the folded
+    FP32 ffn_in, and a copy of ffn_out) into ONE contiguous byte buffer and
+    repoints each layer at views into it; _pin_arena_in_l2() then aims a
+    single CUDA accessPolicyWindow at that buffer with
+    hitProp=Persisting/missProp=Streaming, backed by a
+    cudaLimitPersistingL2CacheSize reservation. See those two methods for
+    why the "FP32 model does not fit in L2" ground-truth figure does not
+    apply to the hot working set, and csrc/l2_persist.cpp for why this is a
+    compiled extension rather than ctypes. Pure memory-layout/caching --
+    every computed value is bit-identical, and if the extension cannot be
+    built the model degrades to G1.6 alone.
     """
 
     def __init__(self, config: TransformerConfig) -> None:
@@ -263,6 +276,11 @@ class UserOptimizedTransformer(BaselineTransformer):
         self._mask_cache: dict = {}
